### Ready-made requests for IntelliJ's HTTP client or VS Code "REST Client".
### Start the stack first: docker compose up --build   (demo accounts are created with these fixed ids)
### Amounts are integer minor units: 2500 = SGD 25.00, 50000 = JPY 50,000.

@base = http://localhost:8080
@alice = 8398f93a-24c5-3661-8e9a-33d54273d824
@bob = 9f75da44-22c8-31e4-9a7d-2bd07518cc4a
@carol = f5da7969-bb24-307c-ad5f-82b42413fc67
@kenji = 413efdce-9786-318b-be29-69819a82091a

### Alice's balance
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### Transfer SGD 25.00 from Alice to Bob (change the key to send a new transfer;
### send it twice with the same key and you get the same transaction back)
POST {{base}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: example-transfer-1

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{alice}}", "destinationAccountId": "{{bob}}", "amount": 2500, "description": "Lunch split" }

### Alice's history (oldest first)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/transactions?page=0&size=50

### Cross-currency: SGD 100.00 from Alice to Carol (USD)
POST {{base}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: example-fx-1

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{alice}}", "destinationAccountId": "{{carol}}", "amount": 10000 }

### Insufficient funds -> 422
POST {{base}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: example-too-much-1

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{bob}}", "destinationAccountId": "{{alice}}", "amount": 999999999 }

### Reverse a transaction (paste an id from a response above)
POST {{base}}/transactions/PASTE-TRANSACTION-ID/reversals
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: example-reversal-1

{ "reason": "Customer dispute" }

### Deposit JPY 10,000 into Kenji
POST {{base}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: example-deposit-1

{ "accountId": "{{kenji}}", "amount": 10000 }

### A deposit from outside, with the outside system's id (e.g. a Fireblocks transaction id).
### Send it again with a NEW Idempotency-Key and the same externalRef -> 409 EXTERNAL_REF_ALREADY_USED
POST {{base}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: example-onchain-deposit-1

{ "accountId": "{{carol}}", "amount": 25000, "description": "Incoming transfer", "externalRef": "fb-tx-example-0001" }

### Current FX rates
GET {{base}}/fx/rates

### Integrity check: totals, chain, every account
POST {{base}}/integrity/checks

### Month-end reconciliation (this month = provisional)
POST {{base}}/reconciliations/month-end?period=2026-10

### Hash-chain head (record it somewhere outside the system)
GET {{base}}/ledger/head

### Integrity hold status (admin)
GET {{base}}/admin/integrity-hold
X-Admin-Key: dev-admin
